# Connect A Signal Bus

This Livebook starts a Bus through an Agent Plugin and routes a published Signal
to the owning Agent.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define The Consumer

```elixir
defmodule BusGuide.Consumer do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "bus_guide_consumer"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{values: Zoi.list(Zoi.integer()) |> Zoi.default([])})

    plugin Jido.Plugin.Bus.Manager, config: [name: :guide_bus]
    plugin Jido.Plugin.Bus.Client, config: [bus: :guide_bus, path: "guide.bus.**"]
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/bus"

    route "guide.bus.record" do
      action %{value: value, observer: observer},
        name: "bus_guide_record",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{value: Zoi.integer(), observer: Zoi.pid()}),
        context: context do
        state = context.agent_state
        send(observer, {:bus_guide_recorded, context.signal.id})
        {:ok, %{state | values: state.values ++ [value]}}
      end
    end
  end
end
```

Manager appears before Client so the Bus exists before subscription setup.

## Start The Consumer

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
jido = Jido.default_instance()

{:ok, consumer} =
  Jido.start_agent(BusGuide.Consumer, id: "bus-consumer")

:ok = Jido.AgentServer.await_ready(consumer)
```

## Publish A Signal

```elixir
signal =
  Jido.Signal.new!(
    "guide.bus.record",
    %{value: 7, observer: self()},
    source: "/guides/publisher"
  )

{:ok, bus} = Jido.Signal.Bus.whereis(:guide_bus, jido: jido)
{:ok, [_record]} = Jido.Signal.Bus.publish(bus, [signal])

receive do
  {:bus_guide_recorded, id} -> id
after
  5_000 -> raise "Bus delivery did not arrive"
end
```

## Read Committed State

```elixir
Jido.AgentServer.agent(consumer).state.values
```

The result is `[7]`. A normal Client uses a cast. It does not acknowledge a
durable cursor.

For durable consumption, set a stable `durable:` ID and a `start_from:` value.
The Client then calls the Agent and acknowledges only after commit. The Agent
must handle duplicate Signals.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(consumer)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

See the [Jido Signal Bus guide](https://hexdocs.pm/jido_signal/) for Store,
replay, cursor, and acknowledgement details.
